  "method": "LD_PRELOAD SIGPROF (ITIMER_PROF) userspace self-PC sampling of unmodified binaries; 500us requested, kernel tick (CONFIG_HZ=1000) limited; no stack attribution, no hardware counters (perf_event_paranoid=4). The `dense` sampler is the repository sampler with the first expiration moved inside the first tick, so no prefix of a short run goes unsampled. A sample inside a shared library counts in `samples` and is reported only as `outside_main_executable`, so libc memcpy/malloc in the LLVM builds is inside that share. LTO inlines many guest functions into their callers, so a sample is attributed to the surviving outer symbol. Every run is pinned to CPU 6 and its output hash is verified; no wall-time claim is made from profiled runs.",
